From ef98b0093acfebabad0ba8d4d60d86e4e26be224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:28:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bt-hf: open the SCO path for the hands-free client role

Incoming-call audio never arrived. The audio HAL client gated the receive path on the
handset role, so nothing fed the SCO stream while this device is the hands-free client;
the state machine and the SCO setup needed the matching adjustments.

The dialer half of this is a product overlay -- config_defaultDialer pointed at a dialer
the product does not install, so no InCallService was bound and neither the call screen
nor the ringtone appeared. This patch only covers the stack.

What the state machine and the audio HAL client changes do not do on their own is start
the HF role's software SCO data path, so with only them the SCO stream still has nothing
at either end. The rest of the stack half:

 - bta_hf_client_main.cc: acquire the HFP software SCO endpoints when the HF role is
   enabled and release them when it is disabled, mirroring the AG role. Without it
   bta_hf_client_sco_datapath_active() never becomes true and every HF branch below it
   is dead code.
 - bta_hf_client_sco.cc: ask for the HCI SCO path through
   hfp_hal_interface::get_offload_enabled() instead of hard-coding offload in the seven
   esco_parameters_for_codec() calls, and stop both sessions when SCO closes.
 - stack/btm/btm_sco_hci.cc: hand the HCI SCO reads and writes to the HF client when its
   data path is active, instead of always to the AG.
 - audio_bluetooth_hw/device_port_proxy.cc: map the SCO output and input devices onto
   HFP_SOFTWARE_ENCODING_DATAPATH / HFP_SOFTWARE_DECODING_DATAPATH. Without it the
   Bluetooth audio HAL refuses the stream ("adev_open_output_stream: cannot init HAL")
   and the policy manager finds no input for the SCO headset.

Measured on the Raspberry Pi 4 board: with the complete set the phone's in-band ringtone
and the call voice both reach the speakers (2026-09-19). Without these four pieces
(2026-09-23) the HAL refuses the SCO stream and Telecom routes the call to the bus
speaker with nothing on it.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
